{"tool_name":"pratt","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"pratt","home":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/jdispatcher/pfa/pratt","summary":"Discover patterns in unaligned protein sequences.","addition_date":"2015-01-29T15:48:06Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T13:57:48.017591Z","tool_type":["Web application","Web service"],"version":["1"],"collections":["EBI Tools","Job Dispatcher Tools"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:pratt","credit":[{"name":"EMBL-EBI","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Inge Jonassen","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"University of Bergen","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Job Dispatcher","typeEntity":"Project","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/jdispatcher"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/jdispatcher/help"},{"type":["Other"],"url":"https://www.ii.uib.no/~inge/Pratt.html"},{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/about/terms-of-use"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["biomadeira","nandana"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"}}],"operation":[{"term":"Sequence motif discovery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0238"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence signature report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2762"}}]}],"name":"Pratt (EBI)","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"jdispatcher","publication":[{"doi":"10.1002/pro.5560040817","metadata":{"abstract":"We present a new method for the identification of conserved patterns in a set of unaligned related protein sequences. It is able to discover patterns of a quite general form, allowing for both ambiguous positions and for variable length wildcard regions. It allows the user to define a class of patterns (e.g., the degree of ambiguity allowed and the length and number of gaps), and the method is then guaranteed to find the conserved patterns in this class scoring highest according to a significance measure defined. Identified patterns may be refined using one of two new algorithms. We present a new (nonstatistical) significance measure for flexible patterns. The method is shown to recover known motifs for PROSITE families and is also applied to some recently described families from the literature. Copyright \u00a9 1995 The Protein Society","authors":[{"name":"Collins J.F."},{"name":"Higgins D.G."},{"name":"Jonassen I."}],"citationCount":248,"date":"1995-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Protein Science","title":"Finding flexible patterns in unaligned protein sequences"},"pmcid":"PMC2143188","pmid":"8520485","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkac240","metadata":{"abstract":"The EMBL-EBI search and sequence analysis tools frameworks provide integrated access to EMBL-EBI's data resources and core bioinformatics analytical tools. EBI Search (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ebisearch) provides a full-text search engine across nearly 5 billion entries, while the Job Dispatcher tools framework (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/services) enables the scientific community to perform a diverse range of sequence analysis using popular bioinformatics applications. Both allow users to interact through user-friendly web applications, as well as via RESTful and SOAP-based APIs. Here, we describe recent improvements to these services and updates made to accommodate the increasing data requirements during the COVID-19 pandemic.","authors":[{"name":"Basutkar P."},{"name":"Edbali O."},{"name":"Kolesnikov A."},{"name":"Lee J."},{"name":"Lopez R."},{"name":"Madeira F."},{"name":"Madhusoodanan N."},{"name":"Pearce M."},{"name":"Tivey A.R.N."}],"citationCount":1248,"date":"2022-07-05T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"Search and sequence analysis tools services from EMBL-EBI in 2022"},"pmcid":"PMC9252731","pmid":"35412617","type":["Other"]},{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkae241","metadata":{"abstract":"The EMBL-EBI Job Dispatcher sequence analysis tools framework (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/jdispatcher) enables the scientific community to perform a diverse range of sequence analyses using popular bioinformatics applications. Free access to the tools and required sequence datasets is provided through user-friendly web applications, as well as via RESTful and SOAP-based APIs. These are integrated into popular EMBL-EBI resources such as UniProt, InterPro, ENA and Ensembl Genomes. This paper overviews recent improvements to Job Dispatcher, including its brand new website and documentation, enhanced visualisations, improved job management, and a rising trend of user reliance on the service from low- and middle-income regions.","authors":[{"name":"Butcher S."},{"name":"Eusebi A."},{"name":"Lee J."},{"name":"Lopez R."},{"name":"Madeira F."},{"name":"Madhusoodanan N."},{"name":"Niewielska A."},{"name":"Tivey A.R.N."}],"citationCount":60,"date":"2024-07-05T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"The EMBL-EBI Job Dispatcher sequence analysis tools framework in 2024"},"pmcid":"PMC11223882","pmid":"38597606","type":["Other"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Sequence sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0160"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Pratt (EBI)","home":"https://bio.tools/pratt","version":"1","summary":"Discover patterns in unaligned protein sequences.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:pratt:1/soap/www.ebi.ac.uk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"terms_of_use":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":76,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"1998"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2014"},{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":2,"